                    "description": "High-NOx endpoint of the upstream `COOxidation: High NOx - Short Chain Length` test (test_co_oxidation.jl:272-303). Same halved radical pool (OH=5.0e11, HO₂=5.0e13) but NO=2.5e17 and NO₂=7.5e17 m⁻³ — two orders of magnitude more NOx. Pins all six outputs at rel=1e-10. L_HOx=3.7645e12 here far exceeds the low-NOx endpoint's 1.395e11, reproducing the upstream L_HOx-grows-with-NOx assertion as a structural fact; chain_length=26.9 > 0. (At this high-NOx point the chain length is longer than at the low-NOx endpoint because the gross-propagation numerator k_HO2_NO·HO₂·NO scales with NO — up 100× — faster than the NO₂-driven OH+NO₂ termination term; the upstream test asserts only chain_length > 0, not a chain-length ordering.)",
