                    "description": "Low corner of the upstream `COOxidation: Qualitative - Positive Production and Loss` 3×3×3 sweep (test_co_oxidation.jl:337-366): OH=1e11, HO₂=1e13, NO=1e14, NO₂=2e14 m⁻³ (CO=2.5e18, O₃=1e18 at defaults). The upstream test asserts L_OH, L_HO2, L_HOx and HO2_ss are all strictly positive at every sweep point — pinned here at rel=1e-10 (L_OH=6.75e10, L_HO2=2.868e10, L_HOx=7.8e8, HO2_ss=7.407e13, all > 0). Note P_O3 is negative here (−1.92e10): at this very low NO the gross HO₂+NO production cannot keep up with the OH+O₃ and HO₂+O₃ ozone-loss channels, so the net O₃ rate is destruction — a regime the upstream qualitative test does not constrain (it checks only the four loss/steady-state outputs).",
